imud-signalk (1.8.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: a bad value in imud-signalk.conf is now fatal,
    where it was previously accepted with no message at any log level.
    A value too long for its field — host, or the stream socket path —
    was truncated and used, so the bridge connected somewhere the
    operator never wrote. An out-of-range integer wrapped, so a
    dest_port of 4294977414 became port 10118. And nan, inf and 1e999
    loaded cleanly into any float key. dest_port and tcp_port are also
    now bounded to 1..65535, because 70000 fits an int perfectly well
    and then becomes port 4464 the moment htons() truncates it.
  * The daemon no longer leaves the binary stream socket bound with
    nothing behind it, so a bridge that connects is either served or
    refused. Previously a daemon whose stream thread failed to start
    still had the socket bound: the bridge connected successfully, into
    the backlog, and then waited forever with no diagnostic at either
    end. See the imud changelog.
  * No wire-format change: the packet stays v17 / 276 bytes.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-signalk (1.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: the bridge now runs with imud as its primary group
    and no longer belongs to gpio. It carried Group=gpio only to reach
    the stream socket — it touches no hardware — and the socket is now
    imud:imud. The bridge connects as the socket's owner either way, so
    this needs no coordinated upgrade and nothing in the bridge's own
    configuration changes.
  * Fix: a config file that exists but cannot be read is now fatal. It
    previously fell through to defaults, and since enabled defaults to
    false the bridge exited reporting "disabled in config
    ([imud-signalk] enabled = false)" — naming the wrong cause entirely
    for what is a permissions problem.
  * Harden: tier-2 systemd sandboxing (empty CapabilityBoundingSet, a
    @system-service syscall allow-list, RestrictNamespaces,
    LockPersonality, RestrictSUIDSGID, ProtectHostname, ProtectClock,
    ProtectProc=invisible, ProcSubset=pid, UMask=0077), and every fd is
    close-on-exec.
  * Requires wire format v17 (packet 276 bytes), unchanged since 1.7.
    Delta output, config keys and CLI are unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-signalk (1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: dest_addr accepted a numeric IPv4 address only, while every
    other bridge resolved its destination with getaddrinfo(3). It now
    uses the same shared helper, so a hostname, an IPv6 address or a
    broadcast address all work. The systemd unit gains AF_INET6 to match
    — without it a hostname resolving to IPv6 failed at socket() under
    the unit's sandbox.
  * Rebuilt for wire format v17 (packet 260 -> 276 bytes); must be
    upgraded together with the daemon. Delta output is unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

