imud-signalk (1.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New udp_enabled key gates the UDP delta output, independent of
    tcp_enabled. BEHAVIOR CHANGE: UDP previously sent whenever the bridge
    ran; add udp_enabled = true to existing configs to keep sending.
    The stock config ships the daemon enabled with every output off.
  * Fix: enabled = false no longer crash-loops under systemd (Type=notify)
    — the bridge signals readiness before exiting cleanly.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-signalk (1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tcp_enabled/tcp_bind_addr/tcp_port keys: serve the same deltas
    newline-framed on a TCP listener (default port 10113) so a Signal K
    server can consume them as a TCP client data connection; UDP output is
    unchanged and keeps sending alongside.

